note OMC-EFF coordinator (PROTOCOL.md, corrected by PROTOCOL-2.md, profile option from PROTOCOL-3.md), the
note Omega port of the former run.sh (OMC-EFF-4). It builds the arms, records provenance and starts the
note Omega conductor; the conductor (conductor.om) does the timing, the output and runtime-line checks and
note the counter reading. It computes no statistics.
note
note   run [--profile P] HERE OMC OUTDIR [CPU]                    baseline: omc, cO2, cO0, neg
note   run [--profile P] --ab HERE BASE CAND SEED OUTDIR [CPU]    A/B: omcB, omcC, cO2, neg
note
note P        om1 (default): kernels/CASE.om, cases named CASE. om2: the committed kernels/om2/CASE.om,
note          cases named om2/CASE on every row (PROTOCOL-3); the same C twins and want/ bytes
note HERE     bench/omc_efficiency (PROTOCOL*.md, conductor.om, kernels/, want/)
note OMC/BASE the omc under test / the baseline omc (also builds the conductor and the neg mutants)
note CAND     the candidate omc (A/B only)
note SEED     the run seed of the A/B, declared in the candidate's evidence before the run (nonzero)
note OUTDIR   a new directory for the work tree and the raw evidence (missing parents are created)
note CPU      the core to pin to (default 19)
note Relative HERE, OMC, BASE, CAND and OUTDIR are made absolute against the working directory; symbolic
note links are not resolved. Host tools run by absolute path with an empty environment: /usr/bin/gcc
note -B/usr/bin/, objdump, size, sha256sum, git, date, uname, lscpu, perf. Pinning uses cpuset/setprio.
note Exit: 0 when every conductor invocation exits 0; 1 when any exits otherwise (the run still goes on,
note and its status is in provenance.txt as build_rc, build_B_rc, build_C_rc, run_rc); 64 bad usage;
note 70 a setup step failed (named on stderr).
om2
